<title>BAHRAIN: Islamic bank unit to to make loans of $39.7 mln.</title>
<headline>Islamic bank unit to to make loans of $39.7 mln.</headline>
<dateline>MANAMA 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Islamic Development Bank's Investment Fund unit said on Wednesday it had agreed to extend $39.7 million in loans to three IDB member states.</p>
<p>It said in a statement that Kuwait would receive $25 million to finance a petrochemical project, Turkey would get $7.5 million to fund the building of an airport and Algeria would receive $7.2 million for a power project.</p>
<p>The unit operates as a vehicle to mobilise funds for the Jeddah-based IDB to boost economic development in member states.</p>
</text>
